 {"id":"fabro-85a1","title":"merge-upstream: full-history clone (run.clone depth=0) - shallow clone broke range math in 3 consecutive merge runs","status":"closed","type":"bug","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-08T18:19:37.228Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T19:45:16.677Z","assignee":"fabro","description":"The shallow-clone trap hit THREE consecutive merge-upstream runs (01M20E43YS, 01M20N60ZY, both merge+reviewer nodes journaled it with 'Do not keep rediscovering this'): the run sandbox clone arrives at depth 100 (.git/shallow boundary e.g. 43036bb477), so git rev-list --count origin/denkhaus..upstream/main reports a misleading ~4919 and git merge-base returns nothing until the merger unshallows mid-pass (~8s). Commit a4850e681 fixed this for the CONDUCTOR survey only ([run.clone] depth = 0 in .fabro/workflows/conductor/workflow.toml) - the merge children are their own workflow and .fabro/workflows/merge-upstream/workflow.toml has NO [run.clone] section, so every merge child still rediscovers the trap. Each child run clones origin/denkhaus fresh at creation (conductor workflow.toml comment).

FIX: add [run.clone] depth = 0 to .fabro/workflows/merge-upstream/workflow.toml, mirroring the conductor commit a4850e681 (volume is ~neutral - the survey's unbounded git fetch upstream already pulls the full shared history into the shallow clone each pass, ~150 MB either way, measured). Alternative considered and rejected: a merger-procedure is-shallow guard + git fetch --unshallow is per-pass remediation, not a fix.

Basis: journals .fabro/journal/01M20E43YS004DCEYPJ0GJQH4B.jsonl and 01M20N60ZY6DZDTX60WW0161KP.jsonl (merge v1 + reviewer v1 painpoints), agent sweep 2026-09-08 evening, commit ccf927888.","labels":["engine"],"closedAt":"2026-09-08T19:45:16.677Z"}
